WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.329 --> 00:00:04.310
The Chinese market has long been a goldmine
for many German companies, with high-end car

00:00:04.310 --> 00:00:09.310
makers like Audi and Mercedies making an ever
larger share of their profits here.

00:00:09.310 --> 00:00:14.150
But the BDI Federation for German Industy
claims the Chinese market is far from a level

00:00:14.150 --> 00:00:15.960
playing field.

00:00:15.960 --> 00:00:21.039
The business lobby accuses Beijing of using
a combination of protectionism, price dumping,

00:00:21.039 --> 00:00:26.420
and state-subsidies to bolster China's economy
and cement the central government's control.

00:00:26.420 --> 00:00:31.920
The development of a free market isn't on
Beijing's agenda.

00:00:31.920 --> 00:00:35.680
The central government is trying to expand
the communist party's control of the economy

00:00:35.680 --> 00:00:41.780
and civil society and that's become more apparent
in the last three years.

00:00:41.780 --> 00:00:47.050
There is also growing concern that China's
shopping tour of buying controlling shares

00:00:47.050 --> 00:00:52.450
of German high-tech companies like robotics
manfaturer Kuka could soon lead to a strategic

00:00:52.450 --> 00:00:54.340
disadvantage for Europe.

00:00:54.340 --> 00:00:59.040
In their report the BDI is calling on Berlin
to take action to make the economies of Germany

00:00:59.040 --> 00:01:00.780
and Euopre more resiliant.

00:01:00.780 --> 00:01:04.660
Among the demands: increased scrutiny of China's
state-support for firms that compete with

00:01:04.660 --> 00:01:07.730
European companies and more oversight of Chinese
acquisitons.

00:01:07.730 --> 00:01:14.610
But the BDI also says western countires must
do more to defend their lead in techonology

00:01:14.610 --> 00:01:20.130
Of course we need to do our own homework and
increase our own competitveness by investing

00:01:20.130 --> 00:01:28.570
more in infrastructure and education including
research by expanding the EU's research budget.

00:01:28.570 --> 00:01:33.750
The BDI also believes EU members must close
ranks to insure China does not eventually

00:01:33.750 --> 00:02:28.480
gain

00:02:28.480 --> 00:03:04.660
a competitive edge

00:03:04.660 --> 00:03:04.840
in tehcnology.

